            "notesHeading": "<div class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Parallax (P) = (a sin A + b cos A) × 955 (mil) R + (a cos A - b sin A)</div><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm font-semibold\">Ratio of conversion of ship roll value to roll correction (T) = 0.28 × H/√(H² + B²) = ------</div>",
            "notesItems": [
              "a. a / aa - Distance between the LRF and Illuminator/ TV camera along the fore and aft line. ('a' is positive if LRF is placed ahead of TV/Illuminator otherwise it is negative).",
              "b. H - Height of LRF rod from Foxle datum mark deck.",
              "c. B - Slant distance from Foxle datum mark to LRF rod.",
              "d. b - It is the perpendicular distance from the fore and aft line to the Illuminator. ('b' is positive for starboard side and negative for port side).",
              "e. R - Range of selected landmark/target as measured by LRF.",
              "f. A - Average bearing of selected landmark/target as measured by the LRF."
